      "id": "finite_key_normalization",
      "root_cause": "taxonomy._matches removes all non-ASCII letters and only splits lowercase-or-digit to uppercase. Explicit Chinese aliases and acronym-to-word transitions are absent.",
      "bounded_fix": "Add versioned finite aliases for unambiguous sensitive keys and acronym-boundary normalization; retain unknown keys and aggregate guards. Do not export keys or treat aliases as confirmed values.",
      "real_prevalence_established": false
    },
    {
      "id": "direct_key_loses_parent_role",
      "root_cause": "structured_types._children passes only current key; user/account plus child id has no recognized one-hop role while direct user_id works. Existing test intentionally fixes noninheritance.",
      "bounded_fix": "Allow only precise parent-role plus direct scalar leaf pairs, such as user/account.id. Keep repo.id, arbitrary name/id, arrays and carrier descendants unresolved without explicit pair rules.",
      "real_prevalence_established": false
    },
    {
      "id": "reference_syntax_and_provenance",
      "root_cause": "The dollar branch in content_types._REFERENCE accepts only a simple variable, so $user.email gets named_value_candidate instead of identifier_reference. Untyped leaf values and aliases are not inspected for one-hop finite source hints.",
      "bounded_fix": "Recognize bounded dotted/bracket identifier reference syntax separately from literal values. Preserve source-role hints only for explicit references; optional one-hop same-document exact alias resolution must retain unresolved/external/cyclic references and never promote to literal or credential validity.",
      "real_prevalence_established": false
    }
  ],
